meta {
  name: Update Channel Products Subpath - Not Supported (Flow 6)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/channels/6aa047d52b6fd055ffb7cadd/products
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "product_ids": ["6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].description: contains extra_forbidden
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 -- `USER_FLOWS.md` Flow 6, against the kept
  channel fixture (read-only probe, nothing mutated).

  ## Resolves the help-center-vs-spec discrepancy Flow 6 flagged
  The help-center says a Channel is a "Destination" with products
  "assigned directly," implying no separate product-list step -- but
  `ChannelCreateInputDto`/`ChannelOutputDto` both have `product_list_id`.
  Testing both candidate mechanisms resolves this:

  - **Direct assignment subpath**: `PATCH /channels/{id}/products` --
    `422`, identical "`products` isn't a real field on
    `ChannelUpdateInputDto`" shape as
    `10-Pim-Product-Lists/Update List Products Subpath - Not Supported
    (Flow 5).bru`. No such mechanism exists.
  - **`product_list_id`**: confirmed in Phase 4a to link immediately on
    create. This is the **only** way products reach a channel via the
    API -- the dashboard's "direct assignment" is UI framing, not a
    distinct mechanism; very likely implemented as an auto-generated
    hidden product list under the hood when a user "directly assigns" in
    the dashboard.

  ## "Process" (Draft → Live) is confirmed UI/internal-only
  `POST /channels/{id}/process` and `.../build` -- both `405 Method Not
  Allowed`. Separately, `PATCH`ing `{"active": true}` on the kept channel
  left `running`/`last_run_start_at`/`file_path` all unchanged
  (still `false`/`null`) -- confirms `active` is just a metadata flag,
  not a build trigger. No v3 endpoint (declared or undeclared) exposes
  the actual export-build action.
}
